// Pools, backoff and flow control, with no I/O of their own.
//
// Each of the three answers a question and leaves the acting to the caller: which
// resource to hand out, how long to wait before trying again, whether this request
// is within the rate. The clock is read by the caller and passed in, and so is the
// randomness backoff jitter needs, which is what makes every sequence here
// reproducible in a test.
//
// The jitter strategies are the ones AWS's "Exponential Backoff and Jitter"
// (https://aws.amazon.com/builders-library/timeouts-retries-and-backoff-with-jitter/)
// names and measures.
import {
  "moonbitstack/moondate",
}
